# .gitignore - Society Management documentation toolchain
#
# Scope: exclude only installed dependencies and build-generated documentation
# artifacts. The following are intentionally NOT ignored so they remain tracked:
#   - authored Markdown sources    docs/**/*.md
#   - source / test trees          src/  tests/
#   - the consolidated deliverable docs/Society-Management-Documentation.pdf
#   - the three rendered diagrams  docs/assets/diagrams/{structure,module-grouping,build-pipeline}.svg
#   - the source archive           society_mgmt_300k.zip
#   - the dependency lockfile      package-lock.json
# Keep this file minimal and scoped; do not add a blanket *.pdf or docs/ ignore.

# Dependencies
# Installed by `npm install` from the documentation toolchain in package.json.
node_modules/

# Logs
# npm / runtime log noise; never part of the documentation deliverable.
# npm-debug.log* also catches rotated logs (e.g. npm-debug.log.1) that *.log misses.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Generated documentation artifacts (rendered by the docs build, then committed)
# `npm run docs:diagrams` renders the three canonical diagrams to SVG here via
# `mmdc` on every build. Those three SVGs are COMMITTED deliverables: the final
# documentation set and the consolidated PDF embed them, and the Markdown
# link-check requires their targets to exist, so each is re-included by an
# explicit negation below. The directory's *other* contents are still ignored
# with a trailing `/*` (rather than the directory itself) so any stray or
# intermediate output stays untracked while the canonical deliverables are
# tracked; git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is wholly
# excluded, which is why the pattern targets the contents (`/*`) and not the
# directory. Scoped narrowly to this directory (no blanket *.svg) to avoid
# touching authored content elsewhere.
docs/assets/diagrams/*
!docs/assets/diagrams/.gitkeep
!docs/assets/diagrams/structure.svg
!docs/assets/diagrams/module-grouping.svg
!docs/assets/diagrams/build-pipeline.svg

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
